{
  "_note": "0.3.127 (E) — role-appropriate lootable gear + ammo on bestiary NPCs. Stamped by tools/bestiary-loot.mjs, which is idempotent: it strips every item flagged flags.draw-steel-ghostwire.loot and re-embeds this table, so the file is the source of truth and a re-run is a no-op. Paths are src/packs/** SKU JSON; quantity defaults to the SKU's own. An actor with no row here carries nothing, and that is a decision, not an omission — see _noLoot.",

  "_noLoot": {
    "beasts": "reach-critters/** and wilds-jungles/** have no pockets. A Scrap-Hound is not carrying a box of rounds.",
    "ice": "wire-machine ICE (Black ICE, Scrambler, Watchdog) and the Signal entities are Wired constructs with no physical body on the map to loot. The two Chrome Raiders DO get loot: they are chromed bodies with real guns bolted on.",
    "risen": "veil-undead skeletons, zombies, ghouls and the Ghost rose without their kit. The Veil Cultist is a live person and is looted.",
    "clubCast": "Most of mama-club is a social scene, not an encounter. A singer, a bartender and three dancing patrons get nothing, because giving a nightclub patron a lockpick set is exactly the filler junk this lock forbids. The five who carry a real object because their own stat block names one are listed."
  },

